rkets its financing products under the CashNetUSA, NetCredit, OnDeck, Headway Capital, Simplic, and Pangea brands. Enova International, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Steven E. Cunningham C.F.A. | CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 13%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $965K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Enova International, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.2B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +17% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 58% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 56 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.90\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -23.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $38.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 90% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Enova Internationa